[e^{-W_k} \hat{\varphi}_j] \in \marsfs{F}^{\,q} \cap \overline{\marsfs{F}}^{\, N_k-q}
\]
which correspond to $[\varphi_i], [\varphi_j] 
\in \Omega(W_k)^{\boldsymbol{\mu}_d}$ under 
the isomorphism \eqref{eq:Hodge-decomp-Jacobi}. 
When $p+q>N_k$, the pairing 
$([e^{-W_k}\hat{\varphi}_i], [e^{-W_k}\hat{\varphi}_j]) =0$ 
vanishes by \eqref{eq:Hodge-Riemann}. 
When $p+q < N_k$, the pairing again vanishes 
because of the Hodge-Riemann bilinear 
relation \eqref{eq:Hodge-Riemann} for $\overline\marsfs{F}$.  
When $p+q = N_k$, we have 
\begin{align*} 
\left( [e^{-W_k}\hat{\varphi}_i], [e^{-W_k}\hat{\varphi}_j] 
\right) & =  \left([e^{-W_k} \varphi_i], [e^{-W_k} \varphi_j]
\right) \quad 
\text{by \eqref{eq:Hodge-Riemann}} 
\\ 
& = \frac{1}{d} 
\Pair{[e^{-W_k} \varphi_i]}{(-1)^{|j|}
[e^{W_k} \varphi_j]} \quad 
\text{by \eqref{eq:FJRW-pairing}} 
\\
& = 
(-1)^{\frac{N_k(N_k-1)}{2}}
(2\pi\mathtt{i})^{N_k} 
\frac{1}{d} 
\operatorname{Res}_{W_k} \left( [\varphi_i], (-1)^{|j|}[\varphi_j]  \right) 
\quad 
\text{by \eqref{eq:G_ij_values}}.  
\end{align*} 
The factor $(-1)^{|j|}$ comes 
from the map $I^*$ in \eqref{eq:Istar}. 
The proof of Proposition \ref{pro:FJRWstatespace_Jacobi} 
is complete.

